 in the form of  intense exercise or lack of sleep but it  can also take  shape from other life experiences and  factors as well  all of which can increase cortisol  levels so look for ways to reduce the  stress in your life by engaging in  relaxing activities  like meditation journaling talk therapy  yoga or other acts of self-care so what  is the bottom line on reversing  metabolic damage  the truth is if you want to improve your  metabolism and  fix metabolic damage after a period of  severe caloric restriction  there are two popular methods to do so  one is the more calculated but  arguably less effective method at  achieving full metabolic restoration  reverse dieting  while the other is more aggressive but  faster and a more thorough approach  the all-in approach gaining weight and  body fat  may be part of the process regardless of  which method you choose  and it may in fact be necessary for  overall health  whichever method you choose to reverse  metabolic adaptation  it's very important that you're working  with a registered dietitian and  if you're coming from an eating disorder  history a full  medical team and that is of course to  ensure that you're not  at risk of refeeding syndrome well folks  that is all for today's video  if you liked it be sure to give it that  thumbs up leave me a comment below if  you have any big  questions that you want me to tackle  subscribe to the channel  and i'll see you next time on abby's  kitchen bye  you

